Log Reading in Remote Servers

When we need to read logs from a remote server, we must first notify the remote server tool to start logging using log-reading test cases (TCS).

Once the request is received by the remote server tool, it should start writing logs using Apache Tailer.

After that, when the verification test cases are received, the remote server should read the created log file and send the result back to the main tool.

There should be a separate endpoint to receive log test case execution requests. This endpoint should not create reports.

When triggering log file collection in the reporting utility method, it should call all remote servers to retrieve their log files. For this purpose, there should also be a separate endpoint.

The log file name and location should be provided as parameter values.

When executing log test cases, we need to store the log file name in Ehcache.
At the end of the test case execution, retrieve the file names from the cache and send requests to the remote servers to fetch the log files.


